      "findingMessages": {
        "naming-app-discord-points-to-github": "The command id `app.discord` (and the `DISCORD` constant in links.rs, labelled \"legacy constant retained for callers\") opens GitHub Issues, not a Discord community; `app.artcraft` opens the Orthic Labs GitHub org and `app.website` the repository. A reader or agent grepping for the Discord link or the website finds the wrong destination, and the id promises a channel the product no longer has.",
        "naming-headless-two-types-one-file": "main.rs imports `lightcraft_mcp::Headless` (an in-process MCP backend session) at module level, then `snapshot()` imports `lightcraft_ui_egui::headless::Headless` (a UI renderer) under the same name, shadowing it; the test at 1055 also uses a bare `Headless::demo()`. Two unrelated types share one identifier in one file (and the CLI also uses mcp's `Remote`, a control-connection backend, while denoise's `Remote` is a tile runner), so adding a second use in either scope silently binds the wrong type.",
        "naming-fit-tone-family-meanings-collide": "`fit_tone` (quantile fit returning a CameraTone), `fit_tone_conditional` (the other CameraTone fit), `fit_tone_with_shadows` (a tone fit variant) and `fit_tone_only` (returns a whole CameraLook with the colour kept) share a prefix but not a return type or meaning; `fit_tone` does not say it is the quantile method although ToneFit::Quantile exists, and `fit_tone_only` reads like the generic tone fit. A caller picking `fit_tone_only` expecting a CameraTone fails to compile at best, or picks the monochrome-only path by mistake."
      },
      "findingTitles": {
        "naming-app-discord-points-to-github": "Rename the ids/constants to what they open (e.g. app.community, app.organization) with an alias table for persisted shortcuts, or document the legacy ids at the HELP_URLS definition.",
        "naming-headless-two-types-one-file": "Alias on import (`use lightcraft_ui_egui::headless::Headless as UiHeadless`) or qualify one of them.",
        "naming-fit-tone-family-meanings-collide": "Name by method and result, e.g. fit_tone_quantile, fit_tone_conditional, and monochrome_tone_look for the CameraLook-returning one."
      },
